{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record, for each failed provider request, its HTTP status and\nprovider error code when the provider reports them, and whether the harness\nretried it. It MUST NOT record the failure's message text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check every obligation in `requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`.\n\n- **Status and code recorded when reported.**\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt]` runs a provider that fails five times with 429 and `ThrottlingException`. It asserts that each failed request's `failure` object equals `{http_status: 429, error_code: \"ThrottlingException\", retried: true}`.\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[permanent_provider_failure_returns_without_waiting_or_retrying]` asserts `{400, \"ValidationException\", retried: false}`.\n  - `src/authoring/usage.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt]` checks `end_request` and the persisted log directly.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failure_codes_are_the_status_and_code_a_provider_reports]` and `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sdk_string_errors_preserve_habeas_provider_reports_and_error_kinds]` check that `failure_codes` extracts the status and code from the provider error.\n- **Not reported.** The `providers.rs` test checks that plain errors and `io::ErrorKind::TimedOut` errors give `(None, None)`. In `end_request`, those `None` values pass straight into the `Option` fields of `RequestFailure` with no branching, so no separate test is needed.\n- **Retried flag, both values.**\n  - `retried: true` is asserted for the retried attempts in the throttled test and after `log.retried(first)` in the usage test.\n  - `retried: false` is asserted in the permanent-failure test and in the usage test before `retried` is called.\n  - The successful sixth request has no `failure` key.\n- **No message text.**\n  - `RequestFailure` has only the fields `http_status`, `error_code` and `retried`.\n  - Every test compares the whole `failure` object with `assert_eq!` against exactly those three keys, so an added message field would fail them.\n  - The permanent-failure test uses an error whose message contains \"Too many tokens\", and the exact comparison still holds.\n\nThe tests do not combine a partial report (a status without a code) with an assertion. That is a variation inside an input class already covered, because both fields are plain `Option`s.",
  "references": "84847014386e817e824449139f8d03f23553c3d0664aef169ade58e9f7184000",
